</svg></figure>
<figure><img src="data:image/png;base64," width="480" height="240" alt="gain"></figure>
<p class="prose">Unity at resonance, whatever the load — the property that makes f0 the design point. Below it the converter boosts, above it it bucks.</p>
<div class="step">nominal(f0)<span class="eq">=</span><span class="subst">nominal(100 kHz)</span><span class="eq">=</span><span class="result">1</span></div>
<div class="step">light(f0)<span class="eq">=</span><span class="subst">light(100 kHz)</span><span class="eq">=</span><span class="result">1</span></div>
<div class="step">heavy(f0)<span class="eq">=</span><span class="subst">heavy(100 kHz)</span><span class="eq">=</span><span class="result">1</span></div>
<p class="prose">Where the nominal curve peaks, and how much gain is there. The slope is exact rather than a difference quotient, so the peak is found by asking where the slope crosses zero.</p>
<div class="step note">fn slope defined</div>
<div class="step"><span class="name">f_peak</span><span class="eq">=</span>roots(slope, f_min_res, f0)<span class="eq">=</span><span class="subst">roots(slope, 44.7214 kHz, 100 kHz)</span><span class="eq">=</span><span class="result">56.0867 kHz</span></div>
<div class="step"><span class="name">M_peak</span><span class="eq">=</span>nominal(f_peak)<span class="eq">=</span><span class="subst">nominal(56.0867 kHz)</span><span class="eq">=</span><span class="result">1.62792</span></div>
<p class="prose">The gain the specification actually demands, at both ends of the input range.</p>
<div class="step"><span class="name">V_bus_min</span><span class="eq">=</span>340 V</div>
<div class="step"><span class="name">V_bus_max</span><span class="eq">=</span>420 V</div>
<div class="step"><span class="name">M_needed_max</span><span class="eq">=</span>n·V_out/V_bus_min<span class="eq">=</span><span class="subst">8.33333·(48 V)/(340 V)</span><span class="eq">=</span><span class="result">1.17647</span></div>
<div class="step"><span class="name">M_needed_min</span><span class="eq">=</span>n·V_out/V_bus_max<span class="eq">=</span><span class="subst">8.33333·(48 V)/(420 V)</span><span class="eq">=</span><span class="result">0.952381</span></div>
<div class="step"><span class="name">margin</span><span class="eq">=</span>M_peak - M_needed_max<span class="eq">=</span><span class="subst">1.62792 - 1.17647</span><span class="eq">=</span><span class="result">0.451451</span></div>
<div class="step"><span class="name">verdict</span><span class="eq">=</span>if margin &gt; 0 then &quot;gain margin available&quot; else &quot;redesign: peak gain too low&quot;<span class="eq">=</span><span class="subst">if 0.451451 &gt; 0 then &quot;gain margin available&quot; else &quot;redesign: peak gain too low&quot;</span><span class="eq">=</span><span class="result">&quot;gain margin available&quot;</span></div>
<p class="prose">The impedance curve, drawn as a magnitude in ohms so the axis is a number.</p>
<div class="step note">fn Z_mag defined</div>
<div class="step note">fn Z_ohm defined</div>
<div class="step">plot(Z_ohm, f_sw_min, f_sw_max)</div>
